   I'm a new hack player and would like to make a few comments about its
difficulty.  Those of you that think that 2.3 was too easy and 3.0 is just
right probably started playing with 2.3.  I am starting with 3.0 and am
finding it extremely frustrating.

   The only way to discover how to play is to experiment.  Apparently 2.3 
was good for this, but after experimentation was done, it was too forgiving.  
Version 3.0 is exteremely unforgiving to the new player.  I have died 
many times while determining which creatures to avoid, how to open stuck 
doors, etc. (the door explodes - you die :-().

   I don't think that making the early levels easier is the answer.  After
spending several months playing Moria, I have all but given up because
it takes too long to get a charactor down to the "fun" levels.  The first
time I played, the early levels were exciting, but now I have worked my way
through them, they are just boring.  That is why I am giving Hack a try.

   I think that a future version of Hack should have different difficulty
levels.  It is too complicated a game for both the beginner and the
expert to fully enjoy without some provision made for their skill.

